{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat CAMPAIGN.md >/tmp/campaign-reread && cat BUDGET.md && cat journal.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PREDICT ---' && nl -ba predict.py | sed -n '1,260p' && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- GIT ---' && git status --short --branch\"","aggregated_output":"# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n\n- Credits: 0.74 / 100.00 USD (1%)\n- Time   : 0.2 h elapsed, 17.8 h remaining (1%)\n- Phase  : normal\n# Research Journal\n\n## Iteration 1 — Starter baseline and volatility diagnosis\n\n- **Hypothesis:** The starter model's standard deviation of every adjacent observed minute return, scaled by square-root time, is miscalibrated because gaps create multi-minute returns treated as one minute and seven-day equal weighting reacts poorly to regime changes. This should hurt both 24h and 1h CRPS, especially on volatile crypto.\n- **Change:** None yet; establish official-backtester baselines at 1000 paths on two post-split regimes, then inspect standardized realized moves. The initially selected 2026-07-10 to 2026-07-12 window produced no archived field prompts: the bundled score history starts on 2026-07-26/27. Valid primary windows are therefore 2026-08-05 to 2026-08-07 and 2026-08-27 to 2026-08-29. Kill threshold for replacing the baseline: candidate must improve mean CRPS on both BTC formats in at least one window and not worsen either competition-level proxy by more than 3% across the second window.\n- **Result:** On 2026-08-05..07, BTC-24h mean CRPS was 1934.45 and BTC-1h was 426.85. On the late window, BTC-24h (2026-08-27..29) was 3433.61, rank 257/257, top-weight ratio 7.3e-13; BTC-1h (2026-08-26..28, shifted one day earlier because a later run requires unavailable 2026-08-30 prices) was 686.62, rank 256/257, top-weight ratio 4.8e-8. Market-only diagnostics showed the 7-day volatility estimate exceeded next-24h realized RMS volatility by roughly 10% in early August and 27% for BTC / 47% for XRP late in August, while a fast/mid/slow EWMA blend was near unit scale.\n- **Verdict:** Discard the starter volatility estimator.\n- **Lesson:** Small raw-CRPS disadvantages become catastrophic after prompt normalization and softmax. Regime adaptation matters more than adding complex path dynamics at this stage. The evaluator must isolate prediction directories and verify horizon coverage to avoid contaminated or out-of-snapshot runs.\n\n## Iteration 2 — Time-decayed gap-aware volatility\n\n- **Hypothesis:** A timestamp-weighted blend of 1-hour, 6-hour, and 24-hour half-life per-minute variance estimates will materially improve both formats by adapting to volatility regimes. Scaling nonconsecutive observed returns by square-root elapsed minutes should also prevent thin assets from treating multi-minute moves as one-minute shocks.\n- **Change:** Replace equal-weight seven-day standard deviation with 45%/40%/15% variance blend at half-lives 60/360/1440 minutes. Preserve the Gaussian random-walk distribution so this iteration isolates volatility estimation. Seed each prompt deterministically to reduce Monte Carlo comparison noise.\n- **Result:** BTC-24h improved from 1934.45 to 1929.29 on 2026-08-05..07. BTC-1h improved from 426.85 to 420.53 on that window and from 686.62 to 641.29 (-6.6%) on 2026-08-26..28. Late BTC-24h on the valid 2026-08-26..28 window was 2969.84 versus a field median near 2891 over the surrounding period. Short-window ranks remain depressed by incomplete moving-average history, so raw CRPS is the decision statistic until 10-day competition runs.\n- **Verdict:** Keep.\n- **Lesson:** Fast variance adaptation captures a large late-regime gain without sacrificing the quieter early window. The next bottleneck is distribution shape and asset heterogeneity, not basic volatility responsiveness.\n\n## Iteration 3 — Cross-asset calibration map\n\n- **Hypothesis:** A single pooled volatility blend is directionally sound but leaves systematic asset-specific dispersion errors, especially for high-coefficient SP500, AAPLX, XAU, GOOGLX, TSLAX, and NVDAX. Mapping official CRPS across assets will identify whether scale calibration should precede tail modeling.\n- **Change:** No simulator change. Replace the evaluator's strict loader with a partition-wise lenient loader that preserves NaNs, then measure one-day 200-path official backtests across all active assets on early- and late-August windows.\n- **Result:** Pending.\n- **Verdict:** Pending.\n- **Lesson:** Pending.\n--- PREDICT ---\n     1\t\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n     2\t\n     3\tUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\n     4\tGenerates predictions from agent/modeling.py over a grid of past prompts (covered by the\n     5\tsnapshot), writes them in the standard format, then scores them with backtest() (validator\n     6\tCRPS + rank vs the real field via the Synth API).\n     7\t\n     8\t--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n     9\t(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\n    10\tgeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\n    11\tfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n    12\t\"\"\"\n    13\t\n    14\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    15\t\n    16\timport argparse\n    17\timport json\n    18\timport os\n    19\timport sys\n    20\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n    21\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    22\t\n    23\timport pandas as pd\n    24\t\n    25\tfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest\n    26\tfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import OHLCV_COLUMNS, STORE_SUBDIR\n    27\t\n    28\t# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n    29\t# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n    30\t# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\n    31\tAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    32\tWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\n    33\tsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n    34\t\n    35\tfrom modeling import simulate  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)\n    36\t\n    37\tCONTEXT_MINUTES = 7 * 24 * 60\n    38\tPREDICTIONS_ROOT = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\"\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n    42\t    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n    43\t\n    44\t    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n    45\t    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n    46\t    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n    47\t    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n    48\t    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n    49\t    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n    53\t    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.\n    54\t\n    55\t    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,\n    56\t    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do\n    57\t    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the\n    58\t    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"\n    59\t    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\tdef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime) -> None:\n    63\t    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n    64\t\n    65\t    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n    66\t    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n    67\t    root = store_root(asset)\n    68\t    missing = []\n    69\t    cursor = start.date()\n    70\t    while cursor <= end.date():\n    71\t        if not (root / f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\").exists():\n    72\t            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n    73\t        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    74\t    if missing:\n    75\t        raise SystemExit(\n    76\t            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n    77\t            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n    78\t            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only) and stops at the campaign's data_cutoff. \"\n    79\t            f\"Reduce --eval-end / --days to stay within the available coverage ({root}).\"\n    80\t        )\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef load_snapshot_range(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    84\t    frames = []\n    85\t    cursor = start.date()\n    86\t    root = store_root(asset)\n    87\t    while cursor <= end.date():\n    88\t        frame = pd.read_parquet(root / f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\")\n    89\t        frames.append(frame[[\"timestamp\", *OHLCV_COLUMNS]])\n    90\t        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    91\t    data = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)\n    92\t    data[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(data[\"timestamp\"], utc=True)\n    93\t    data = data.sort_values(\"timestamp\").drop_duplicates(\"timestamp\")\n    94\t    mask = (data[\"timestamp\"] >= pd.Timestamp(start)) & (\n    95\t        data[\"timestamp\"] <= pd.Timestamp(end)\n    96\t    )\n    97\t    return data.loc[mask].set_index(\"timestamp\")\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tdef generate(\n   101\t    asset: str,\n   102\t    start: datetime,\n   103\t    end: datetime,\n   104\t    cadence_minutes: int = 60,\n   105\t    time_increment: int = 300,\n   106\t    time_length: int = 86_400,\n   107\t    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n   108\t    predictions_dir: Path | None = None,\n   109\t) -> int:\n   110\t    if predictions_dir is None:\n   111\t        predictions_dir = PREDICTIONS_ROOT / \"predictions\"\n   112\t    prices = load_snapshot_range(\n   113\t        asset, start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end\n   114\t    )[OHLCV_COLUMNS]\n   115\t    predictions_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   116\t    end_ts = pd.Timestamp(end)\n   117\t    n = 0\n   118\t    for t in pd.date_range(start, end, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", tz=\"UTC\"):\n   119\t        if t >= end_ts:\n   120\t            break\n   121\t        context = prices.loc[:t][-CONTEXT_MINUTES:]\n   122\t        out = simulate(\n   123\t            asset=asset,\n   124\t            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n   125\t            time_increment=time_increment,\n   126\t            time_length=time_length,\n   127\t            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n   128\t            context_prices=context,\n   129\t        )\n   130\t        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]\n   131\t        payload = {\n   132\t            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),\n   133\t            \"asset\": asset,\n   134\t            \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n   135\t            \"time_length\": time_length,\n   136\t            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),\n   137\t            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),\n   138\t            \"paths\": paths,\n   139\t        }\n   140\t        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n   141\t        (predictions_dir / name).write_text(json.dumps(payload))\n   142\t        n += 1\n   143\t    return n\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\tdef main() -> None:\n   147\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   148\t    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")\n   149\t    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)\n   150\t    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, must be <= data_cutoff\")\n   151\t    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n   152\t    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n   153\t    ap.add_argument(\n   154\t        \"--num-simulations\",\n   155\t        type=int,\n   156\t        default=1000,\n   157\t        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"\n   158\t        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"\n   159\t        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",\n   160\t    )\n   161\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n   162\t    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n   163\t    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n   164\t    start = end - timedelta(days=args.days)\n   165\t    predictions_dir = (\n   166\t        PREDICTIONS_ROOT\n   167\t        / f\"{args.asset}_{args.time_length}_{start.date()}_{end.date()}_{args.num_simulations}\"\n   168\t        / \"predictions\"\n   169\t    )\n   170\t    # the context reaches back 7 days before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far\n   171\t    check_snapshot_coverage(\n   172\t        args.asset,\n   173\t        start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES),\n   174\t        end + timedelta(seconds=args.time_length),\n   175\t    )\n   176\t    n = generate(\n   177\t        args.asset,\n   178\t        start,\n   179\t        end,\n   180\t        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n   181\t        time_length=args.time_length,\n   182\t        num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n   183\t        predictions_dir=predictions_dir,\n   184\t    )\n   185\t    print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")\n   186\t    result = backtest(\n   187\t        miner_name=\"campaign\",\n   188\t        asset=args.asset,\n   189\t        time_length=args.time_length,\n   190\t        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n   191\t        n_backtest_days=args.days,\n   192\t        predictions_dir=predictions_dir,\n   193\t        eval_end=end,\n   194\t    )\n   195\t    print(\"summary:\", result.summary)\n   196\t    if not result.smoothed_scores.empty:\n   197\t        final_time = result.smoothed_scores[\"updated_at\"].max()\n   198\t        final_scores = result.smoothed_scores.loc[\n   199\t            result.smoothed_scores[\"updated_at\"] == final_time\n   200\t        ].copy()\n   201\t        miner_row = final_scores.loc[final_scores[\"miner_uid\"] == 999]\n   202\t        if not miner_row.empty:\n   203\t            final_scores[\"rank\"] = final_scores[\"reward_weight\"].rank(\n   204\t                ascending=False, method=\"min\"\n   205\t            )\n   206\t            row = final_scores.loc[miner_row.index[0]]\n   207\t            top_weight = float(final_scores[\"reward_weight\"].max())\n   208\t            reward_weight = float(row[\"reward_weight\"])\n   209\t            print(\n   210\t                \"final:\",\n   211\t                {\n   212\t                    \"rank\": int(row[\"rank\"]),\n   213\t                    \"miners\": len(final_scores),\n   214\t                    \"reward_weight\": reward_weight,\n   215\t                    \"top_weight\": top_weight,\n   216\t                    \"top_ratio\": reward_weight / top_weight if top_weight else 0.0,\n   217\t                },\n   218\t            )\n   219\t\n   220\t\n   221\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   222\t    main()\n--- GIT ---\n## master\n?? BUDGET.md\n?? ../uv.lock\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
